# Schedule definitions for thorn PlanesX

# PlanesX_Startup registers an IO method (CCTK_RegisterIOMethod) whose
# OutputGH callback writes the planes. CarpetX::OutputGH traverses the
# registered IO methods after all of its built-in writers -- that is, after
# the CCTK_POSTSTEP and CCTK_ANALYSIS traversals (analysis-bin grid functions
# are up to date) and on every iteration including recovery -- and before its
# OutputMeta, so files registered via OutputMeta_RegisterOutputFile are
# described in the same iteration's metadata. This requires the CarpetX
# io-method traversal (commit "CarpetX: call registered IO methods from
# OutputGH"); without it the callback is never invoked and no planes are
# written -- PlanesX_CheckOutputCalled turns that into a hard error.
SCHEDULE PlanesX_Startup AT startup
{
  LANG: C
} "Register the 2D plane output method (Silo and openPMD)"

SCHEDULE PlanesX_CheckOutputCalled AT terminate
{
  LANG: C
  OPTIONS: global
} "Error out if plane output was requested but the IO method never ran"
